ert\nL114: \nL115: cite61†thu-ml / cite62†TetraJet-v2-NVFP4Training Public\nL116: \nL117:   * cite63†Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL118:   * cite63†Fork 0 L119:   * cite63†Star L120:   * cite62†Code L121:   * cite64†Issues 0 L122:   * cite65†Pull requests 0 L123:   * cite66†Actions L124:   * cite67†Projects L125:   * cite68†Security and quality 0 L126:   * cite69†Insights L127: \nL128: Additional navigation options\nL129: \nL130: master\nL131: \nL132: cite70†Branches cite71†Tags L133: \nL134: [Input: Go to file]\nL135: \nL136: Go to file\nL137: \nL138: Code\nL139: \nL140: Open more actions menu\nL141: ## Latest commit\nL142: \nL143: \nL144: \nL145: ## History\nL146: \nL147: 13 Commits\nL148: \nL149: ## Folders and files\nL150: \nL151: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL152: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL153: cite72†kernels | cite72†kernels |    |\nL154: cite73†olmo2-training | cite73†olmo2-training |    |\nL155: cite74†scripts | cite74†scripts |    |\nL156: cite75†.gitignore | cite75†.gitignore |    |\nL157: cite76†LICENSE | cite76†LICENSE |    |\nL158: cite77†NOTICE | cite77†NOTICE |    |\nL159: cite78†README.md | cite78†README.md |    |\nL160: ## Repository files navigation\nL161: \nL162:   *   * cite79†README L163:   * cite79†Apache-2.0 license L164: \nL165: More items\nL166: # TetraJet-v2: Accurate NVFP4 Training for LLMs\nL167: with Oscillation Suppression and Outlier Control\nL168: \nL169: Yuxiang Chen, Yifan Liu, Xiaoming Xu, Pengle Zhang, Michael Beyer, Martin Rapp, Jun Zhu, Jianfei Chen\nL170: \nL171: Tsinghua University & Bosch AI Research\nL172: \nL173: * * *\nL174: \nL175: This repository contains the official implementation of TetraJet-v2, a method for accurate NVFP4 training for large language models with oscillation suppression and outlier control.\nL176: ## Related Information\nL177: \nL178:   * Paper (TetraJet-v2): cite80†arXiv†arxiv.org , cite81†OpenReview†openreview.net L179: \nL180:   * Status:\nL181: \nL182:     * 🎉 (2026/05) This work has been accepted as a Spotlight paper in ICML 2026.\nL183:     * (2026/05) We released an updated version of TetraJet-v2 with kernels and the training recipe.\nL184:     * (2025/10) We released the first version of TetraJet-v2 on arXiv.\nL185:   * Previous work (TetraJet-MXFP4Training, ICML 2025): cite82†arXiv†arxiv.org , cite83†code L186: This work (TetraJet-v2) extends our prior low-bit training efforts (TetraJet) from MXFP4 for ViTs to more accurate and robust NVFP4 training for LLMs.\nL187: ## Core Contributions\nL188:   1. Practically optimal NVFP4 linear recipe: an end-to-end FP4 training recipe with double-block quantization, aligned activations for correct gradient estimation, and the best backward RHT setting for LLM linear layers.\nL189:   2. ⭐ OsciReset (key algorithmic contribution): a lightweight weight-oscillation suppression algorithm that identifies unstable FP4 weights and resets their master weights to quantization-bin centers. It improves weight-optimization stability during annealing and convergence in large-data, long-horizon low-precision training, and can also transfer to Quantization-Aware Training (QAT) for producing low-precision weights.\nL190:   3. OutControl: an outlier-control recipe that combines backward RHT and mixed FP4+MXFP8 outlier-channel retention for more accurate activation and gradient computation.\nL191: TetraJet-v2 improves FP4 pre-training on OLMo2 models up to 370M parameters and reduces the average gap to BF16 by 51.3% over prior FP4 methods, while providing end-to-end speedups over FP8 baselines.\nL192: ## Quick View of This Repo\nL193:   * `olmo2-training/`: OLMo2 training code based on cite84†allenai/OLMo , with files not needed for training removed.\nL194:     * Main OLMo changes are in `olmo/config.py`, `olmo/model.py`, `olmo/train.py`, `scripts/train.py`, plus checkpoint/initialization compatibility for quantized layer buffers.\nL195:     * NVFP4 linear layers are implemented in `olmo/quantization_real/linear.py`.\nL196:     * Mixed NVFP4+MXFP8 outlier-channel training is implemented in `olmo/quantization_real/linear_mix.py` and scheduled by `olmo/quantization_real/calibrate.py`.\nL197:     * Oscillation reset algorithm is implemented in `olmo/quantization_real/oscillation_reset.py` and `olmo/quantization_real/oscillation_reset_memeff.py`.\nL198:   * `kernels/`: TetraJet-v2 NVFP4 kernels.\nL199:   * `scripts/`: local and SLURM launch scripts for OLMo2 training.\nL200: ## Quick Start\nL201: \nL202: ### Prerequisites\nL203: \nL204:   * NVIDIA Blackwell GPU. The TetraJet-v2 kernels were designed for RTX 5090 / RTX PRO 6000.\nL205:   * CUDA >= 12.8\nL206:   * FlashAttention 2.\nL207: ### Install\nL208: \nL209:     conda create -y -n tjv2-nvfp4 python=3.12 pip\nL210:     conda activate tjv2-nvfp4\nL211: \nL212:     # Install OLMo and training dependencies.\nL213:     cd olmo2-training\nL214:     pip install -e \".[train]\"\nL215:     cd ..\nL216: \nL217:     # Install TetraJet-v2 kernels.\nL218:     cd kernels\nL219:     pip install -e . --no-build-isolation\nL220: \nL221: Possible Issues:\nL222:   * Use `--no-build-isolation` when installing CUDA extension packages after PyTorch is installed.\nL223:   * If using a prebuilt FlashAttention wheel, make sure its Python, PyTorch, CUDA, and CXX11 ABI tags match your environment.\nL224:   * Limit CUDA/C++ build parallelism if needed: `export MAX_JOBS=4`.\nL225: ### Data Preparation\nL226: \nL227: The training configs expect OLMo2 preprocessed `.npy` data. You can use the train and eval/perplexity file lists in the official OLMo config cite85†OLMo2-7B-stage1.yaml to download the preprocessed files directly.\nL228: \nL229: After downloading, replace both the training data prefix and the eval data paths in `olmo2-training/configs/*/*.yaml` with your local data directories.\nL230: ### Training\nL231: \nL232: Run launch scripts from `scripts/`:\nL233: \nL234:     cd scripts\nL235: \nL236:     # Local, 1 node, 8 GPUs.\nL237:     ./local_70m_8gpu.sh TJv2-mix_fp8-osci_reset-mem_eff\nL238: \nL239:     # SLURM, 1 node, 8 GPUs.\nL240:     sbatch slurm_70m_1node.sh TJv2-mix_fp8-osci_reset-mem_eff\nL241: \nL242:     # SLURM, 2 nodes, 8 GPUs per node.\nL243:     sbatch slurm_70m_2nodes.sh TJv2-mix_fp8-osci_reset-mem_eff\nL244: Use the corresponding `70m`, `150m`, or `370m` script for each model size. Available config names:\nL245: \nL246:     `bf16\nL247:     TJv2-base\nL248:     TJv2-mix_fp8\nL249:     TJv2-mix_fp8-osci_reset\nL250:     TJv2-mix_fp8-osci_reset-mem_eff\nL251:     `\nL252: \nL253: If no config is provided, scripts default to `bf16`. Pass a checkpoint path as the second argument to resume:\nL254: \nL255:     ./local_70m_8gpu.sh TJv2-base /path/to/checkpoint\nL256: Outputs are saved to `olmo2-training/outputs/<model_size>/<config_name>`. W&B runs offline by default; change `WANDB_MODE` in `scripts/common.sh` to sync online.\nL257: ### Benchmarking Kernels\nL258: \nL259: > See `kernels/README.md`.\nL260: \nL261: ## License\nL262: \nL263: This repository is released under the cite76†Apache License 2.0 .\nL264: \nL265: The `olmo2-training/` directory contains code adapted from cite84†allenai/OLMo , which is also licensed under Apache License 2.0. We retain the upstream license notice and document the TetraJet-v2 modifications in cite77†NOTICE .\nL266: ## Citation\nL267: If you find this work useful, please consider citing:\nL268: \nL269:     @inproceedings{\nL270:         chen2026tetrajetv,\nL271:         title={TetraJet-v2: Accurate {NVFP}4 Training for Large Language Models with Oscillation Suppression and Outlier Control},\nL272:         author={Yuxiang Chen and Yifan Liu and Xiaoming Xu and Pengle Zhang and Michael Beyer and Martin Rapp and Jun Zhu and Jianfei Chen},\nL273:         booktitle={Forty-third International Conference on Machine Learning},\nL274:         year={2026},\nL275:         url={https://openreview.net/forum?id=7ZQhm5HnOA}\nL276:     }\nL277: ## About\nL278: \nL279: [ICML 2026 Spotlight] Official implementation of TetraJet-v2: Accurate NVFP4 Training for LLMs, with fully-NVFP4 linear layer with unbiased backprop, and algorithms to overcome LLMs' weight-oscillation and activation-outlier bottlenecks.\nL280: \nL281: ### Resources\nL282: \nL283: cite86†Readme L284: \nL285: cite87†Apache-2.0 license L286: \nL287: cite88†Activity L288: \nL289: cite89†Custom properties L290: \nL291: ### Stars\nL292: \nL293: 18 stars\nL294: \nL295: ### Watchers\nL296: \nL297: 1 watching\nL298: \nL299: ### Forks\nL300: \nL301: cite90†0 forks L302: \nL303: cite91†Report repository L304: \nL305: ## Releases\nL306: \nL307: ## Packages\nL308: \nL309: ## Contributors\nL310: ## Languages\nL311: \nL312: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n"
